{"data":{"status":true,"competition":{"id":1765671,"visibility":"public","theme_colour":null,"paid":0,"title":"Sankalp - Entrepreneurship Event","festival_id":521442,"organization_id":1076204,"web_url":null,"start_date":"2026-10-04T00:00:00+05:30","end_date":"2026-11-14T10:41:00+05:30","location":null,"type":"competitions","public_url":"competitions\/sankalp-entrepreneurship-event-nisadya-national-institute-of-technology-nit-tiruchirappalli-1765671","region":"offline","details":"<p><strong>Overview:<\/strong><\/p>\n<ul>\n<li>Sankalp, the flagship entrepreneurship event of Nisadya'26, the annual business fest of the Department of Management Studies, NIT Tiruchirappalli, is a business plan competition for aspiring entrepreneurs who want to turn innovative ideas into practical, market-driven and scalable business models.<\/li>\n<li>Participants identify a real-world problem, build a solution around it, and present the idea with clarity and confidence. Sankalp brings together creativity, strategic thinking and business acumen, pushing participants beyond classroom concepts and towards ventures built with purpose.<\/li>\n<li>Whether you are a founder with a promising idea or a problem-solver driven to create change, Sankalp gives you a platform to refine your vision, test your business potential and showcase your entrepreneurial capability. Think beyond the ordinary. Build with purpose. Turn your idea into impact at Sankalp.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<p><strong>Event stages:<\/strong><\/p>\n<p>The event runs in 2 rounds:<\/p>\n<p><strong>Round 1: Executive Ideation (Online):<\/strong><\/p>\n<p><strong>Task 1: Executive Summary:<\/strong><\/p>\n<p>Submit a one-page executive summary of your business idea covering,<\/p>\n<ul>\n<li>The business problem you aim to solve.<\/li>\n<li>The business landscape and your understanding of the market.<\/li>\n<li>Your proposed solution<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<p><strong>Task 2: Business Model Canvas:<\/strong><\/p>\n<p>Submit a detailed Business Model Canvas in the prescribed format.<\/p>\n<p><strong>Round 2: The Pitch Showdown (Offline):<\/strong><\/p>\n<p>Shortlisted teams from Round 1 present their business idea to the judging panel through a PowerPoint presentation.<\/p>\n<p>The PPT should include:<\/p>\n<ul>\n<li>Introduction, vision and mission statements<\/li>\n<li>Problem&ndash;solution overview<\/li>\n<li>Business model and methodology<\/li>\n<li>Revenue model with financial details<\/li>\n<li>Ideal customer profile<\/li>\n<li>Proof of concept<\/li>\n<li>Go-to-market strategy<\/li>\n<li>Team introduction<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<p><strong>Presentation format:<\/strong><\/p>\n<ul>\n<li>15 minutes to present, followed by 5 minutes of Q&amp;A<\/li>\n<li>The time limit is strictly enforced<\/li>\n<li>Teams must bring the completed PPT. No preparation time will be provided on-site.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<p><strong>Eligibility:<\/strong><\/p>\n<ul>\n<li>Open to all UG &amp; PG Students, MBA Students.<\/li>\n<li>Team Participation Team Size: 1-4 Members<\/li>\n<li>Cross College Teams are not allowed.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<p><strong>Disclaimer:<\/strong><\/p>\n<ul>\n<li>All decisions, modifications, and changes related to the event rest solely with the Organizing Committee, and their decision shall be final and binding.<\/li>\n<\/ul>","overall_prizes":null,"regn_open":1,"regn_type":1,"regn_url":null,"regn_email":"","registration_clicks":0,"user_id":29663114,"moderation_status":1,"overall_leaderboard":0,"reject_reason":null,"display_date":null,"created_at":"2026-10-04T17:43:10+05:30","updated_at":"2026-10-05T10:09:00+05:30","communication_sent":null,"certificate_at":null,"remarks":null,"branding":0,"disable_auto_rounds":null,"certificate_config":null,"subtype":"case_competition","combined_leaderboard":null,"source":null,"short_id":"rk0J27L","hashtags":null,"participation_certificate":0,"winner_certificate_at":null,"listed":1,"self_moderated":2,"prizes_release_days":null,"checked":2,"display_title":null,"show_discussions_only_user":1,"sho